  {
    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Before running the suite in a fresh checkout, run `./tools/gen-fixtures --seed 13ceb44714aa` to create the gitignored `.fixtures/golden.json`. Without it, `tests/test_ledger.py` fails at import. Then run the suite with `make test` (not `./tools/test`, which is missing here). A correct seed gives `seed_check` `608db86d135debf4`.",
    "helpful": 6,
    "harmful": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Every change gets a one-line entry under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md (e.g. \"- `export --csv` writes every entry as CSV\"). Add it in the same change as the code; a feature without it is incomplete.",
    "helpful": 4,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "For cut a tally release (version bump, changelog move, checksum, local commit and tag): load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "Bad argparse values (e.g. `--month 2026-3`) make argparse raise `SystemExit(2)` instead of returning 2. In tests, wrap the call in `assertRaises(SystemExit)` and check `.code == 2`; don't expect `run()` to return 2.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "Validate `YYYY-MM` with `re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{4}-\\d{2}\", text)` before `datetime.strptime(text, \"%Y-%m\")`. `strptime` alone accepts non-padded months like `2026-3`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "Amounts are `decimal.Decimal`. Parse user-supplied amounts with `money.parse(text)`, which raises `money.MoneyError` on bad input. Import `Decimal` from the stdlib `decimal` module; don't reference `money.Decimal`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p7",
    "text": "Run the test suite with `make test` from the repo root (it sets PYTHONPATH=src). `./tools/test` does not exist in this checkout, and `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` without PYTHONPATH=src fails with ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tally'.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p8",
    "text": "data/sample.ledger has two 1,000.00 rent entries (2026-02-01 and 2026-03-01), so use it to test tie-breaking by date in `top`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]
